{
  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA, PCA-2000, singleprofile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while config_010 (image, ResNet50, singleprofile) achieves only 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality by a wide margin. With only two data points, the key uncertainty is whether the RNA representation itself is the bottleneck—PCA is a linear, unsupervised projection, and a learned encoder (scVI) may capture nonlinear structure that PCA misses. Question tested: config_004 changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while keeping model_setting=rna_only, profile_setting=singleprofile, and no aggregation, making it a clean single-variable comparison against config_001. Why this is the best next experiment: it isolates the effect of representation learning on the strongest modality. If scVI substantially improves over PCA, it signals that learned encoders are a high-value design axis and justifies further investment in scgpt/multimodal variants. If it does not, PCA is likely near the ceiling for this task and effort is better spent on profile/aggregation or fusion. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most impactful design choice before committing budget to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

